# Permissions

For each entity, a role-based permissions matrix must be established:
- On the permissions page, instead of a datatable, there is a checkbox matrix where at the top of the matrix there is a select dropdown with the roles.
When a role is selected, the permissions for each entity (Rows) and their actions (Columns) are activated or deactivated.
- The possible actions on entities are:

-- View
-- Create
-- Edit
-- View Item (This means whether the entity item is even visible in the sidebar)
-- Delete
-- Edit Own
-- Delete Own

Because of this "own" characteristic, each entity in the system must ALWAYS have the created_by pointing to the user who created the record.

